{
    "background_story": "In a realm beyond mortal comprehension, Atreus, a majestic Griffin, was said to possess the essence of the great playwright Edward Albee. Legend has it that Albee's wit and clever wordplay had been infused into Atreus's being, allowing the Griffin to weave complex tales that could mesmerize even the most skeptical of creatures. Atreus would often perch atop a ancient, gnarled tree, surveying the land below as he composed his masterpieces. His stories were said to be as sharp as his talons, cutting through the noise of the world to reveal the deepest truths. Those who listened to Atreus's tales would be forever changed, their perspectives broadened by the Griffin's Albee-inspired wisdom.",
